    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: the incendiary rules of engagement hold a flame (CE-3486 flame FL-2, F-9 approved R-3111; docs/designs/weapons/DESIGN_Flame_Weapons.md). On basic-desert, two holds, each beside a CONTROL given the same order without the reason to hold: (1) 'Flamer' (a FlamethrowerSoldier, FireAtTarget) faces 'Target A' 20 m east while 'Civilian Beyond' (neutral) stands 10 m behind the target - inside the 40 m flame though off a bullet's line to the target: as Protocol III, no flame with a civilian in it; its control 'Flamer Clear' faces 'Target C' with nobody behind. (2) 'Forbidden Tank' (an M67 whose ROE says IncendiaryForbidden) is ordered to flame the spot where 'Target B' stands; its control 'Allowed Tank' gets the same order at 'Target D'. Judge: the Flamer and the Forbidden Tank never spend fuel and Target A, Target B and the civilian are never hurt; the two controls spend fuel and set their targets alight."
  },
